Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile a comprehensive report with the findings:

## Findings Report: About Page Hero Section Issues

Based on my thorough exploration of the NINEONELABS renewal project, I can now provide a complete analysis of both issues.

---

### **Issue 1: `.no-sub-about-hero-slogan__title` Width Reflow on Scroll**

#### **HTML Structure** (`views/pages/about/index.php`, lines 114-148)

The title wrapper and its content are:

```html
<div class="no-sub-about-hero-slogan__title">
  <h2 class="f-display-x --fm-en"
      aria-label="We lead your design, development, branding, and UI/UX journey.">

    <!-- Line 1: WE LEAD YOUR (keyword) -->
    <span class="no-sub-about-hero-slogan__line mask-target">
      <span class="weak">WE</span>
      <span class="weak">LEAD</span>
      <span class="weak">YOUR</span>

      <!-- Rotating keyword container -->
      <span class="no-sub-about-hero-slogan__keyword-shell" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="no-sub-about-hero-slogan__bracket">(</span>

        <!-- THE CRITICAL ELEMENT: viewport with dynamic width -->
        <span class="no-sub-about-hero-slogan__keyword-viewport">
          <span class="no-sub-about-hero-slogan__keyword-track">
            <span class="no-sub-about-hero-slogan__keyword">DESIGN</span>
            <span class="no-sub-about-hero-slogan__keyword">DEVELOPMENT</span>
            <span class="no-sub-about-hero-slogan__keyword">BRANDING</span>
            <span class="no-sub-about-hero-slogan__keyword">UI/UX</span>
          </span>
        </span>

        <span class="no-sub-about-hero-slogan__bracket">)</span>
      </span>
    </span>

    <!-- Line 2: JOURNEY -->
    <span class="no-sub-about-hero-slogan__line mask-target">
      JOURNEY
    </span>
  </h2>
</div>
```

#### **SCSS Rules Affecting the Title** (from `resource/scss/pages/_sub.scss`, lines 164-332)

**Container:**
```scss
.no-sub-about-hero-slogan__title {
  text-align: center;

  h2 {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: fluid(8, 16);        // 8px to 16px gap between lines
    line-height: 0.9;         // CRITICAL: tight line-height
  }

  .line {
    text-align: center;
  }
}
```

**The Keyword Viewport (CAUSES WIDTH REFLOW):**
```scss
.no-sub-about-hero-slogan__keyword-viewport {
  position: relative;
  display: inline-block;
  height: 0.98em;
  width: auto;              // ← PROBLEM: auto width allows content to drive size
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  overflow: hidden;         // Clips content when width shrinks
  vertical-align: top;
  will-change: width;       // Optimizes for width animation
}

.no-sub-about-hero-slogan__keyword-track {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  transform: translate3d(0, 0, 0);
  will-change: transform;
}

.no-sub-about-hero-slogan__keyword {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  min-height: 0.98em;       // Each keyword has fixed height
  opacity: 0.4;
  filter: blur(8px);
  text-shadow: 0 0 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0);
  will-change: opacity, filter, text-shadow;
}
```

**The Bracket Elements:**
```scss
.no-sub-about-hero-slogan__keyword-shell {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: fluid(10, 18);       // Gap between ( keyword )
  color: var(--clr-white-100);
  white-space: nowrap;      // Prevents line breaks
}

.no-sub-about-hero-slogan__bracket {
  color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--clr-white-100) 72%, transparent);
  font-weight: 400;
}
```

**Parent Line Container:**
```scss
.no-sub-about-hero-slogan__line {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  gap: fluid(10, 18);       // Gap between WE, LEAD, YOUR, (keyword)
  .weak {
    opacity: 0.4;
  }
}

.no-sub-about-hero-slogan__line.mask-target {
  display: block;           // Changes from inline-flex to block

  > .masking-text {
    display: block;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  > .masking-text > .masking-text__line {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: fluid(10, 18);
  }
}
```

#### **How the Width Changes On Scroll**

The width animation is driven by **TypeScript in `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/manager/AppManager.ts`** (lines 368-418):

1. **Configuration** (`resource/ts/config/component.config.ts`, lines 214-230):
```typescript
export const ABOUT_HERO_SLOGAN: Readonly<AboutHeroSloganConfig> = {
  viewportSelector: ".no-sub-about-hero-slogan__keyword-viewport",
  trackSelector: ".no-sub-about-hero-slogan__keyword-track",
  keywordSelector: ".no-sub-about-hero-slogan__keyword",
  keywordCount: 4,           // DESIGN, DEVELOPMENT, BRANDING, UI/UX
  progressWindowStart: 0.08,
  progressWindowEnd: 0.92,
  duration: 0.42,
  ease: "power3.out",
  // ... visual state configs
};
```

2. **The Width Calculation** (`AppManager.ts`, lines 411-418):
```typescript
private _resolveAboutHeroSloganKeywordWidth(
  track: HTMLElement,
  step: number,
): number {
  const keyword = this._resolveAboutHeroSloganKeywordElement(track, step);
  if (!keyword) return 0;
  return Math.max(keyword.scrollWidth, keyword.getBoundingClientRect().width, 1);
}
```

3. **Applied to DOM** (`AppManager.ts`, lines 387-392):
```typescript
gsap.to(viewport, {
  width: keywordWidth,      // ← Animated width from keyword's actual rendered width
  duration: ABOUT_HERO_SLOGAN.duration,  // 0.42s
  ease: ABOUT_HERO_SLOGAN.ease,
  overwrite: true,
});
```

**The Problem:** Each keyword (`DESIGN`, `DEVELOPMENT`, `BRANDING`, `UI/UX`) has different rendered widths. When scrolling, the viewport width animates from one keyword's width to the next. Combined with:
- `overflow: hidden` on the viewport
- `line-height: 0.9` on the h2 (very tight)
- `gap: fluid(10, 18)` (responsive gaps around the viewport)

The container's total width changes, forcing the h2 to reflow between 2 and 3 lines of text.

---

### **Issue 2: "JOURNEY" Word Moves/Peeks When Scrolling**

#### **Location in Markup**

Line 144-146 in `views/pages/about/index.php`:
```html
<span class="no-sub-about-hero-slogan__line mask-target">
  JOURNEY
</span>
```

The word "JOURNEY" is the second `.no-sub-about-hero-slogan__line` element, which means it's the second row of the h2.

#### **Why It Moves on Scroll**

The `h2` uses:
```scss
h2 {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  gap: fluid(8, 16);        // Responsive gap between lines
  line-height: 0.9;
}
```

When the above line's width changes (the keyword viewport expands/contracts), the **`h2` recalculates its flex layout**, which can cause:

1. **Vertical shift**: If the first line wraps to 3 lines vs. 2 lines, the gap spacing and line-height compression affect where the second line (JOURNEY) positions itself
2. **Horizontal peek**: If the first line's width expands significantly (e.g., "DEVELOPMENT" is wider than "DESIGN"), the JOURNEY text may visually appear to shift right due to the flex container's `align-items: center` centering relative to a wider first line
3. **Masking animation**: The `.mask-target` class triggers reveal animations via `mask-target[data-mask="ready"]` (from `state/_reveal-state.scss`, line 12-15), which adds opacity/visibility transitions that may compound the movement illusion

#### **Masking SCSS** (`resource/scss/components/_masking-text.scss`)

```scss
.mask-target {
  opacity: 0;
  visibility: hidden;        // Hidden until TS sets data-mask="ready"
}

.mask-target[data-mask="ready"] {
  opacity: 1;
  visibility: visible;       // Becomes visible during scroll
}

.masking-text {
  display: block;
  overflow: hidden;

  .masking-text__line,
  .line {
    display: block;
    position: relative;
    text-align: start;
    transform: translate3d(0, var(--text-reveal-offset-y), 0);
    opacity: 0;
    filter: blur(var(--text-reveal-blur));
    transition:
      transform var(--transition-slow),
      opacity var(--transition-slow),
      filter var(--transition-slow);
  }
}
```

No `clip-path` rules are applied. The movement is purely from **flexbox reflow** + **`overflow: hidden`** on the viewport + **opacity/visibility state transitions**.

---

### **Summary of CSS/Width Rules Causing Reflow**

| Element | Rule | Impact |
|---------|------|--------|
| `.no-sub-about-hero-slogan__keyword-viewport` | `width: auto` + `overflow: hidden` + animated width via GSAP | Causes container width to change on scroll, triggering h2 reflow |
| `.no-sub-about-hero-slogan__keyword-viewport` | `display: inline-block` | Participates in parent flex layout width calculation |
| `h2` | `gap: fluid(8, 16)` | Responsive gap changes with viewport width on mobile |
| `h2` | `line-height: 0.9` | Very tight, amplifies line-wrapping sensitivity |
| `h2` | `align-items: center` | Centers the entire flex content, including JOURNEY |
| `.no-sub-about-hero-slogan__line` | `display: inline-flex` → `display: block` (when `.mask-target`) | Layout mode change during reveal |
| `.mask-target` | `opacity: 0` → `opacity: 1` | Fade-in animation on JOURNEY during scroll |

---

### **File Paths for Reference**

- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/scss/pages/_sub.scss` — Lines 164-332
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/views/pages/about/index.php` — Lines 108-153
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/scss/components/_masking-text.scss` — Full file (masking base styles)
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/scss/state/_reveal-state.scss` — Lines 12-15 (mask-target ready state)
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/scss/style.scss` — Lines 75-79 (pages layer import)
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/manager/AppManager.ts` — Lines 222-249, 368-418 (width animation logic)
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/config/component.config.ts` — Lines 214-230 (hero slogan config)

